Wave accounting:

- Documents discovered: approximately 30.
- Documents opened: 15 accessible pages, reports, or PDFs.
- Accepted: 8 new source-claim units.
- Reused: 1 prior USTR energy record.
- Rejected or discovery-only: search snippets, duplicate versions of the same report, and sources lacking sufficiently precise attribution.
- Access-blocked: ASF audit index/PDF pages returned internal errors and were not accepted.
- Distinct organizations: IMF, OECD, USTR, World Bank, CONEVAL, INEGI-linked official statistics.
- Source types: multilateral assessments, official statistical releases, national inequality assessments, foreign trade-authority statements, and PDF reports.

Lens coverage is substantive for 5B.1, 5B.3, 5B.4, 5B.6, 5B.8, 5B.9, and 5B.10; partial for 5B.5 and 5B.7; and residual for 5B.2. The main unresolved gaps are direct evidence on economic appointments and delegated authority, procurement favoritism or anti-corruption enforcement, the government’s internal correction of mistaken policies, project-level cost-benefit performance, and the distribution of benefits by region and household type. A narrowly targeted follow-up using SHCP budgets, Banxico communications, ASF audits, CONEVAL/INEGI microdata, and Pemex/CFE financial records would have material value; another broad macroeconomic search would add little.
